This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'b' of validator-arm-selection, and it inherits that fixture's reason without
restating it: its subject is the `--arms` selection mode of scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
and the arm-boundary grammar scripts/render-invariant-index.sh serves it. Neither script is
installed — install.sh copies core/scripts/ to scripts/ai-dlc/, and both of these live in this
repository's own repo-root scripts/ directory, which reaches no consumer at all.

A shard is a scheduling boundary, never a subject boundary, so it can carry no ship decision
its sibling does not. On a consumer this directory would resolve no validator and no renderer,
and could only report that it found nothing to select.
